WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Receive the input
INPUT Minutes; minutes = int(input()); Entered value: 30
The supplied Python input line stores the entered whole number.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Translate the condition
IF Minutes &lt;= 30 THEN; if minutes &lt;= 30:; 30 &lt;= 30 -&gt; True
Keep &lt;= so exactly 30 minutes belongs to this branch.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Store the lower charge
Charge &lt;- 2;     charge = 2
Python uses = for assignment, with indentation inside the branch.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Keep the alternative
else:;     charge = 5; Skipped when minutes = 30
The else branch runs only when the condition is false.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Output after either branch
OUTPUT Charge; print(charge); Output: 2
The unindented print runs after the selected assignment.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Try the next whole minute
minutes = 31; 31 &lt;= 30 -&gt; False; charge = 5; output 5
Testing both sides of the boundary catches &lt; versus &lt;= errors.
